<title>USA: New York City Industrial Development priced.</title>
<headline>New York City Industrial Development priced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said Tuesday that it tentatively priced $107 million of New York City Industrial Development Agency industrial development revenue bonds for 1991 Japan Airlines Company Ltd. project, with a top yield of 6.05 percent in 2015.</p>
<p>The bonds are FSA insured.  </p>
<p>NEW YORK CITY INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT ADENCY</p>
<p>RE: $107,500,000*</p>
<p>INDUSTRIAL DEVELOPMENT REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(1991 JAPAN AIRLINES COMPANY, LTD. PROJECT)</p>
<p>				SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa EXP		   S&amp;P: AAA EXP</p>
<p>     UNDERLYING A2	    UNDERLYING BBB+</p>
<p>FSA INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 11/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 05/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 11/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>11/01/2015	    107,500M    6.05  %</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 11/01/2004 at 102.00, DTP 11/01/2008.</p>
<p>The award is expected Tuesday, October 29, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on November 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Morgan Stanley &amp; Co. Incorporated</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan Securities Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
